After obtaining a ring of slow digestion from a magic lamp in the
mines, the horrible problem with vampire pcs went away and all the
benefits kicked in.  This character was very hard to kill, with
regeneration flying and level drain resistance all built in (plus that
level drain bite isnt bad either).  He ravaged through the mines and
sokoban, and almost got to the quest...   Then he ran into a lightning
bug... bye bye slow digestion.
  The loss of a ring turned a fairly reasonably paced game into a game
of sheer bloodlust for about 14 more levels in a constant need to keep
hunger at bay,  A vampire barbarian flying around with Cleaver,
chopping and hacking, the lightning bug caused much second hand
killing.
  Finally around the wyrm caves another ring was found.  The bloodlust
could be put aside for some real treasure gathering.  before getting to
one eyed sam GDSM a cloak of protection, GoP, and hawiian t-shirt were
all found.
One eyed Sam fell to the Deathsword and two of his own Invulnerability
potions (perhaps he shoulda kept those locked up).  Thus with
reflection and sams better enchanted armor and speed boots, the
ascension kit was nearly complete.  After a couple of offerings to an
aligned altar and no stormbringer, a quick prayer brought about being
crowned Glory of Arioch (and strombringer)
  A wand of Death was found in the spider caves (Girtab lived a short
life as a pet before a quick death at the whimsical hand of
Stormbringer)... the wand used to kill all of the Disgruntled
adventurers guild.   At this point I had a complete ascension kit and
hadnt even gotten to the castle yet, and more wands potions and scrolls
than I could carry even in my bag of holding.
  At about this point all the scrolls and potions were put to use, a
couple of
smoky potions wishes made, and 30 total creatures genocided (all L's
c's h's x's (goodbye lit bug) and ;'s for good measure)... vampire
mages were later genocided (on the vibrating square level) for their
annoying summon nasty ability, and their frequent spawning.
  Demogorgon proved the next big challenge, used up 9 potions of full
healing 3 scrolls of scare monster and 5 potions of paralyze, along
with a wish for a ring of free action (forgot mine upstairs), before I
gave up on the paralyze and ran for the upstairs that I had left a
scroll of scare monster on. Demogorgon was surely anticipating an easy
win and was just as surprised as I to find I had killed him (hadnt been
able to get the unicorn horn enchanted by this point).
  The only other major problem was the planetars showing up on the
plane of air (guess they could've been solars), but another potion of
invulnerability and that problem was gone.  Death was an easy kill...
and pestilence fell to one of the 5 wands of death I carried.  never
had to fight famine thankfully... I didnt know what I'd do as a
vampire. (cant really carry food easily and never found a medical kit)
killed rodney 7 times.


Goodbye thorium the Demigod...


